WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.291
Hi! Welcome back to Nagarjuna.

00:00:07.291 --> 00:00:10.851
And we've reached the sixth class.

00:00:10.851 --> 00:00:15.469
I'd like to show you a
picture which sums up

00:00:15.469 --> 00:00:18.150
what we talked about last time.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:21.817
And here you can see a
lady cleaning the floor.

00:00:21.817 --> 00:00:26.521
And this comes from an
actual event at my house

00:00:26.521 --> 00:00:29.571
where I kept walking out
into the kitchen at night

00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:31.411
to get a glass of water or something,

00:00:31.411 --> 00:00:33.582
and I would step in a puddle of water.

00:00:33.582 --> 00:00:35.650
So turn on the light, get a cloth,

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:38.851
clean up the puddle of
water, get my glass of water,

00:00:38.851 --> 00:00:40.571
go back to bed.

00:00:40.571 --> 00:00:43.371
And this went on night after night.

00:00:43.371 --> 00:00:46.561
And every night, I would
patiently get on my knees

00:00:46.561 --> 00:00:48.742
and clean up the puddle of water.

00:00:48.742 --> 00:00:53.393
And then finally after
about three weeks, I'm like,

00:00:53.393 --> 00:00:56.491
"Hey, maybe it's coming from somewhere."

00:00:56.491 --> 00:00:58.862
I was like, "Duh!"

00:00:58.862 --> 00:01:00.521
And I looked under the sink.

00:01:00.521 --> 00:01:02.611
I guess, subconsciously,

00:01:02.611 --> 00:01:04.960
I really didn't want
to look under the sink

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.930
because it's so scary down there.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:09.273
There's so much weird stuff down there

00:01:09.273 --> 00:01:10.940
that I threw down there

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:12.822
and I didn't want to go through the sink

00:01:12.822 --> 00:01:15.631
and find out everything was soaked.

00:01:15.631 --> 00:01:17.381
But I did and it was.

00:01:18.702 --> 00:01:22.035
The idea of Buddhism... it's very beautiful.

00:01:23.689 --> 00:01:27.921
You don't attack the result,
you attack the cause.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:32.274
So you don't fix things
by fixing the result.

00:01:32.274 --> 00:01:34.418
You fix things by fixing the cause.

00:01:34.418 --> 00:01:37.751
Fixing the result would be something like,

00:01:39.081 --> 00:01:41.507
cleaning the puddle up every night.

00:01:41.507 --> 00:01:44.394
But you didn't fix the source.

00:01:44.394 --> 00:01:46.647
You didn't fix the cause of it

00:01:46.647 --> 00:01:48.404
and then it's just going to come back again.

00:01:48.404 --> 00:01:52.321
So the idea is: attack the
cause. Find the source

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:54.569
and attack that.

00:01:54.569 --> 00:01:58.449
We just talked about
steps that have brought

00:01:58.449 --> 00:02:00.744
about the problems in our lives,

00:02:00.744 --> 00:02:04.596
starting with a tendency that we brought

00:02:06.275 --> 00:02:07.108
into this life with us, with our mind,

00:02:07.108 --> 00:02:11.245
to see things as coming from themselves.

00:02:11.245 --> 00:02:14.328
And then that's going
to trigger this habit

00:02:14.328 --> 00:02:19.245
of thinking that 'me' and
'mine' come from themselves.

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:23.355
And then that's going to
trigger this habit of liking

00:02:23.355 --> 00:02:26.119
the things that seem good,

00:02:26.119 --> 00:02:28.458
disliking the things that seem bad,

00:02:28.458 --> 00:02:31.599
and then reacting to them
and responding to them.

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:33.882
Fighting for getting more of what I like,

00:02:33.882 --> 00:02:36.848
fighting against people I don't like,

00:02:36.848 --> 00:02:40.590
and then making more karma to
plant more seeds in my mind

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:42.759
to carry on into my next life

00:02:42.759 --> 00:02:44.740
for the circle to continue again.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:48.407
So we don't struggle
with, for example, money.

00:02:50.963 --> 00:02:52.840
We don't struggle with money.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:55.240
We don't struggle with current money.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.823
We invest for future money

00:02:56.823 --> 00:02:58.362
and that's all we do.

00:02:58.362 --> 00:02:59.649
We don't fight.

00:02:59.649 --> 00:03:04.149
We don't compete for current
existing amounts of money.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.186
We don't do that in this system.

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:10.436
We plant the seeds that will grow money

00:03:11.732 --> 00:03:14.931
a couple of weeks later
or couple of months later.

00:03:14.931 --> 00:03:18.914
So we address the problem at the source

00:03:18.914 --> 00:03:22.295
and we don't address the
problem at the result.

00:03:22.295 --> 00:03:27.203
And that's the idea. So don't
forget "the sink thing."

00:03:27.203 --> 00:03:31.836
Just to remind you, in this
chapter so far, we were supposed

00:03:31.836 --> 00:03:33.655
to be covering five things.

00:03:33.655 --> 00:03:38.128
Number one was, how do you get
into understanding emptiness?

00:03:38.128 --> 00:03:40.378
And we finished that section.

00:03:41.951 --> 00:03:43.580
There were five sections.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.951
the third section — I'll
skip the second one — 

00:03:45.951 --> 00:03:50.344
was, how do you teach
someone about emptiness?

00:03:50.344 --> 00:03:54.844
The fourth section was, what's
the essence of emptiness?

00:03:56.427 --> 00:03:58.094
The fifth section is,

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:01.116
how do you put that into practice?

00:04:01.116 --> 00:04:03.903
But the second section, which is what

00:04:03.903 --> 00:04:05.561
we are going to cover today,

00:04:05.561 --> 00:04:07.494
is called LUNG DANG 'GAL SPONG.

00:04:07.494 --> 00:04:10.160
LUNG DANG 'GAL SPONG means,

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.423
"Hey, Nagarjuna! I like your ideas,

00:04:13.423 --> 00:04:18.423
"they seem pretty interesting.
They are pretty persuasive,

00:04:18.553 --> 00:04:22.166
"but aren't you contradicting
what Lord Buddha said?"

00:04:22.166 --> 00:04:24.189
Because Lord Buddha did say

00:04:24.189 --> 00:04:26.023
that things had a nature of their own.

00:04:26.023 --> 00:04:28.746
He said they do have a nature of their own.

00:04:28.746 --> 00:04:30.454
And he did.

00:04:30.454 --> 00:04:34.037
So then Nagarjuna is
stuck in this position

00:04:34.037 --> 00:04:37.454
which he was hard stuck into in which book?

00:04:39.229 --> 00:04:43.810
"The Sixty Verses," which
Nick Lashaw is translating.

00:04:43.810 --> 00:04:46.768
Like, you have to address the times

00:04:46.768 --> 00:04:50.351
early in the Buddha's career when he said,

00:04:50.351 --> 00:04:53.407
"Yes, things do have a
nature of their own."

00:04:53.407 --> 00:04:55.296
And now we've got to talk about that.

00:04:55.296 --> 00:04:58.740
So, here's Nagarjuna's response.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:00.506
,BDAG GO ZHES KYANG BTAGS GYUR CING,

00:05:00.506 --> 00:05:02.231
,BDAG MED CES KYANG BSTAN PAR GYUR,

00:05:02.231 --> 00:05:03.456
,SANGS RGYAS RNAMS KYIS BDAG DANG NI,

00:05:03.456 --> 00:05:05.939
,BDAG MED 'GA' MED CES KYANG BSTAN,

00:05:06.832 --> 00:05:08.898
He says, "When you think about it,

00:05:08.898 --> 00:05:10.628
"there's three options here."

00:05:10.628 --> 00:05:11.948
What are the three?

00:05:11.948 --> 00:05:13.939
,BDAG GO ZHES KYANG BTAGS,

00:05:15.198 --> 00:05:19.543
Yes, the Buddha said, "There
is a self nature to things."

00:05:19.543 --> 00:05:23.816
He did historically say,
"Things do have a self nature."

00:05:23.816 --> 00:05:24.935
He did say that.

00:05:24.935 --> 00:05:29.185
But the verb here is not
say. The verb here is 'BTAGS',

00:05:30.221 --> 00:05:35.054
which means fantasize. (laughs)

00:05:35.054 --> 00:05:38.354
So yes, Buddha did kind of fantasize

00:05:38.354 --> 00:05:40.608
about a self nature.

00:05:40.608 --> 00:05:45.124
There was a period in his life
when Buddha was fantasizing

00:05:45.124 --> 00:05:46.287
about a self nature.

00:05:46.287 --> 00:05:48.889
We'll see what this means later.

00:05:48.889 --> 00:05:51.073
But then there was another
part of his life when

00:05:51.073 --> 00:05:54.252
,BDAG MED CES KYANG BSTAN PAR GYUR,

00:05:54.252 --> 00:05:57.352
But there was another part
of his life where he said,

00:05:57.352 --> 00:06:01.323
"You know, things also
don't have a self nature."

00:06:01.323 --> 00:06:05.992
So he qualified. Things also
don't have a self nature.

00:06:05.992 --> 00:06:08.041
Then at the end, he said

00:06:08.041 --> 00:06:09.632
,SANGS RGYAS RNAMS KYIS BDAG DANG NI,

00:06:09.632 --> 00:06:12.092
,BDAG MED 'GA' MED CES KYANG BSTAN,

00:06:12.092 --> 00:06:15.812
Later he said, "It's not true
that things have a self nature

00:06:15.812 --> 00:06:20.123
and it's not true that they
don't have a self nature."

00:06:20.123 --> 00:06:21.336
So we've got three options here.

00:06:21.336 --> 00:06:25.172
In the early part of his
teaching career, Buddha said...

00:06:25.172 --> 00:06:29.589
Buddha fantasized about a
self nature that was there.

00:06:31.037 --> 00:06:33.241
Later he said, "You can take your choice,

00:06:33.241 --> 00:06:38.128
take it or leave it: self
nature or no self nature."

00:06:38.128 --> 00:06:39.961
He taught two options.

00:06:40.983 --> 00:06:42.483
Then in the third...

00:06:45.441 --> 00:06:46.274
Sorry. RNAMS KYIS BDAG DANG NI,

00:06:46.274 --> 00:06:48.822
,BDAG MED 'GA' MED CES KYANG BSTAN,

00:06:48.822 --> 00:06:52.248
He also taught... I'm sorry.
The third option was

00:06:52.248 --> 00:06:54.068
it's not true that there is a self

00:06:54.068 --> 00:06:57.318
and it's not true that there is no self.

00:06:58.372 --> 00:07:02.888
Let me say it again. First
he said there is a self.

00:07:02.888 --> 00:07:06.624
And he went like this, there is a "self".

00:07:06.624 --> 00:07:09.404
Then he said, "You know
there is a way you can think

00:07:09.404 --> 00:07:11.133
if there is a self or there is no self."

00:07:11.133 --> 00:07:13.591
And then later he said,
"No, there is no self

00:07:13.591 --> 00:07:16.124
and there's not no self."

00:07:16.124 --> 00:07:19.029
So this Nagarjuna, he's being cute,

00:07:19.029 --> 00:07:21.675
he really enjoys being cute.

00:07:21.675 --> 00:07:23.628
So I thought it'd be
worth it to go through

00:07:23.628 --> 00:07:27.009
these ideas separately, which
is going to slow us down

00:07:27.009 --> 00:07:29.040
in a certain way.

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:30.130
But I'm not really excited.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:31.891
Here is the commentary.

00:07:31.891 --> 00:07:33.507
SANGS RGYAS RNAMS KYIS
NI MDO SDE 'GA' ZHIG TU

00:07:33.507 --> 00:07:35.098
BDAG GO ZHES KYANG

00:07:35.098 --> 00:07:36.257
BDAG YOD PAR BTAGS PAR

00:07:36.257 --> 00:07:39.741
GYUR PA STE BSTAN PA LTAR GSUNGS

00:07:39.741 --> 00:07:43.523
There was a time in the
Buddha's career when he said,

00:07:43.523 --> 00:07:48.065
"Yes, there does exist a
self nature to things."

00:07:48.065 --> 00:07:49.429
He said that.

00:07:49.429 --> 00:07:50.971
First choice. Second choice:

00:07:50.971 --> 00:07:55.571
YANG 'GA' ZHIG TU NI, RANG
RKYA THUB PA'I BDAG MED DO

00:07:55.571 --> 00:07:58.432
Then he said KYANG BSTAN.

00:07:58.432 --> 00:08:01.408
He said, "On top of
there being a self nature,

00:08:01.408 --> 00:08:05.383
"there's also in some cases
a lack of a self nature."

00:08:05.383 --> 00:08:06.937
He gave an option.

00:08:06.937 --> 00:08:09.920
What was the lack of the
self nature he talked about?

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:12.987
In those days, it was the lower emptiness

00:08:12.987 --> 00:08:16.702
of the lower schools, which just means

00:08:16.702 --> 00:08:20.756
a self nature which is independent,

00:08:20.756 --> 00:08:22.912
which doesn't depend on other things.

00:08:22.912 --> 00:08:25.521
So the lower form of emptiness

00:08:25.521 --> 00:08:29.660
is sort of like there's a driver.

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:30.840
You guys remember that?

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:34.631
RANG RKYA THUB PA'I RDZAS YOD KYIS STONG

00:08:34.631 --> 00:08:39.614
Someone's in control. Someone
can be in current control.

00:08:40.944 --> 00:08:44.317
You can get more money by
doing these things immediately

00:08:44.317 --> 00:08:46.900
and not by being generous.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:50.988
So he said there's no such 
thing as that kind of money.

00:08:50.988 --> 00:08:53.920
And finally: YANG 'GA' ZHIG
TU BDAG DANG BDAG MED PA 'GA'

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:56.629
YANG RANG BZHIN GYIS GRUB PA MED DO

00:08:56.629 --> 00:09:00.536
There is neither a self
nature nor no self nature

00:09:00.536 --> 00:09:05.044
where both of those come
from their own side.

00:09:05.044 --> 00:09:06.591
There is no self,

00:09:06.591 --> 00:09:08.964
and there is no lack of a self nature,

00:09:08.964 --> 00:09:10.405
but I'm only talking about ones

00:09:10.405 --> 00:09:13.077
that come from their own side.

00:09:13.077 --> 00:09:14.410
So that's three.

00:09:17.106 --> 00:09:19.491
What's the goal of this section?

00:09:19.491 --> 00:09:22.206
We're trying to explain why
Buddha seemed to have said

00:09:22.206 --> 00:09:24.194
there was a self nature to things

00:09:24.194 --> 00:09:25.777
and we end up saying

00:09:25.777 --> 00:09:30.610
he were just saying different
things to different people.

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:34.577
Who did he say those things to?

00:09:34.577 --> 00:09:35.960
RIM PA BZHIN DU BLO DMAN DAG LAS

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:38.209
'BRAS LA SKUR BA MI 'DEBS PA DANG

00:09:38.209 --> 00:09:41.222
First of all, he did say
there was a a self nature

00:09:41.222 --> 00:09:44.055
to people of lowest spiritual intellect

00:09:44.055 --> 00:09:47.323
because he wanted to make sure

00:09:47.323 --> 00:09:50.247
that they didn't discount karma

00:09:50.247 --> 00:09:51.843
and its consequences.

00:09:51.843 --> 00:09:54.807
So he wanted to say, "You
do have a self nature

00:09:54.807 --> 00:09:56.515
"and things are going to come back to you

00:09:56.515 --> 00:09:58.660
"if you do bad things."

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:02.026
So he was afraid if he
said there is no self,

00:10:02.026 --> 00:10:05.536
people would go ahead and be naughty.

00:10:05.536 --> 00:10:07.567
So he said, "No, that self exists.

00:10:07.567 --> 00:10:10.565
"The one who gets back all
the trouble he gave to others,

00:10:10.565 --> 00:10:12.658
"that one exists."

00:10:12.658 --> 00:10:14.974
Because he wanted them to be good people.

00:10:14.974 --> 00:10:19.432
Second: 'JIG LTA LHOD PA

00:10:19.432 --> 00:10:21.027
He told other people,

00:10:21.027 --> 00:10:22.860
"Well, you know, in some
ways there's a self

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:24.319
"and other ways there is no self."

00:10:24.319 --> 00:10:27.806
And that's to help people
overcome the attitude

00:10:27.806 --> 00:10:32.312
about the bottle of
water which is mistaken.

00:10:32.312 --> 00:10:36.129
That 'me' and 'mine'
come from the outside.

00:10:36.129 --> 00:10:40.167
Then, who did he give
the last explanation to?

00:10:40.167 --> 00:10:43.834
Neither self nor no self
comes from themselves.

00:10:45.648 --> 00:10:47.381
Who did he give that to?

00:10:47.381 --> 00:10:49.581
ZAB MO'I DON RTOGS NUS PA'I GDUL BYA

00:10:49.581 --> 00:10:54.172
He reserved that for students
who were extraordinarily

00:10:54.172 --> 00:10:58.172
sensitive and were able
to get the deeper truth.

00:10:59.239 --> 00:11:02.579
So yes, did he change
his message about self?

00:11:02.579 --> 00:11:03.543
Yes.

00:11:03.543 --> 00:11:05.685
Did he contradict himself about the self?

00:11:05.685 --> 00:11:07.160
No.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:09.835
Because it was very intentional.

00:11:09.835 --> 00:11:11.205
He revealed different layers

00:11:11.205 --> 00:11:14.024
of selflessness according to the capacity

00:11:14.024 --> 00:11:15.565
of the students.

00:11:15.565 --> 00:11:17.648
That covers that section.

00:11:18.707 --> 00:11:20.873
Three kinds of me's. You've got it here?

00:11:20.873 --> 00:11:23.540
I don't know... what was that.

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:26.960
We don't have to have that picture.

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:29.754
BSHAD TSUL GCIG LA

00:11:29.754 --> 00:11:31.895
And I'm sorry to going
into all this detail

00:11:31.895 --> 00:11:34.395
but it's just beautiful to me.

00:11:36.308 --> 00:11:37.751
He says, "There is also a way in which

00:11:37.751 --> 00:11:40.174
"you can explain these two differently."

00:11:40.174 --> 00:11:42.340
Some people explain
these three differently.

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:43.340
He says, what?

00:11:45.773 --> 00:11:49.538
He was trying to get along
with the Sāṃkhya.

00:11:49.538 --> 00:11:51.840
He was trying to get along with followers

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:54.994
of the religion into which he was born.

00:11:54.994 --> 00:11:58.690
And he said, "Of course
there's a self nature,

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:01.514
"it's inherent in all things.

00:12:01.514 --> 00:12:03.506
"There is a big self who
creates all things."

00:12:03.506 --> 00:12:05.839
He's trying not to freak out...

00:12:06.921 --> 00:12:09.202
like Jesus among the
Jewish people or something.

00:12:09.202 --> 00:12:12.477
He was trying to be cooperative
with who he grew up with.

00:12:12.477 --> 00:12:14.898
That's one interpretation when it says

00:12:14.898 --> 00:12:18.470
he did claim there was a self.

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:20.986
Second: RGYANG BAN PAS PHYI MAR

00:12:20.986 --> 00:12:23.657
'GRO 'ONG BYED PA'I BDAG MED DO

00:12:23.657 --> 00:12:27.574
And then there was a school
called the Charvakas,

00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:33.714
who said there was nobody
to go on into a future life.

00:12:33.714 --> 00:12:36.289
And he said, "No, that self there is."

00:12:36.289 --> 00:12:37.572
You will take a future.

00:12:37.572 --> 00:12:39.988
There is somebody who takes a future

00:12:39.988 --> 00:12:40.821
life, trust me.

00:12:40.821 --> 00:12:44.189
But he was just talking in that context.

00:12:44.189 --> 00:12:45.022
SANGS RGYAS BCOM LDAN 'DAS
RNAMS KYIS NI BDAG DANG BDAG

00:12:45.022 --> 00:12:48.033
MED PA 'GA' YANG RANG
BZHIN GYIS GRUB PA MED DO

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:52.718
And then finally, in his
ultimate presentation,

00:12:52.718 --> 00:12:54.926
he said, "Уes, there is that 'me',

00:12:54.926 --> 00:12:56.677
"yes, there is that 'mine',

00:12:56.677 --> 00:13:01.366
but they do not come from
their own side." That's all.

00:13:01.366 --> 00:13:02.866
Next section.

00:13:04.841 --> 00:13:08.258
I like this section. This is pretty famous.

00:13:10.696 --> 00:13:14.012
DON DAM PAR BRJOD MI NUS PA'I RGYU MTSAN

00:13:14.012 --> 00:13:16.912
DON DAM PAR BRJOD MI NUS PA'I RGYU MTSAN

00:13:18.745 --> 00:13:20.995
In the Vajrayogini sadhana:

00:13:22.446 --> 00:13:23.837
BRJOD LAS 'DAS,
BRJOD DU MED PA

00:13:25.754 --> 00:13:29.569
'Beyond words',
'Beyond description'

00:13:29.569 --> 00:13:33.378
The reality of the world
is beyond all words.

00:13:33.378 --> 00:13:36.201
And now that subject is going to come up.

00:13:36.201 --> 00:13:38.080
DON DAM PAR BRJOD MI NUS PA'I RGYU MTSAN

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:43.080
Why is it that emptiness is
said to be indescribable?

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:44.796
If it's indescribable, why would we have

00:13:44.796 --> 00:13:48.996
to study this long book
describing it? (laughs)

00:13:48.996 --> 00:13:51.213
If emptiness is really indescribable,

00:13:51.213 --> 00:13:55.227
why we got to do all this
hard work to describe it.

00:13:55.227 --> 00:13:59.394
So Nagarjuna, thankfully - I
think sensitively for us - 

00:14:00.328 --> 00:14:01.323
he's going to say,

00:14:01.323 --> 00:14:05.338
"Yes, we do say emptiness
is indescribable.

00:14:05.338 --> 00:14:08.582
"Yes, we do say you can't
describe it in words,

00:14:08.582 --> 00:14:10.922
"but that has a special meaning."

00:14:10.922 --> 00:14:12.497
And here's the next verse:

00:14:12.497 --> 00:14:13.713
,BRJOD PAR BYA BA LDOG PA STE,

00:14:13.713 --> 00:14:14.546
,SEMS KYI SPYOD YUL LDOG PAS SO,

00:14:14.546 --> 00:14:15.887
,MA SKYES PA DANG MA 'GAGS PA,

00:14:15.887 --> 00:14:18.837
,CHOS NYID MYA NGAN 'DAS DANG MTSUNGS,

00:14:18.837 --> 00:14:20.754
Then he says here:

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:26.558
,BRJOD PAR BYA BA LDOG PA STE, 

00:14:26.558 --> 00:14:31.141
Yeah, it cannot be immediately
expressed in words.

00:14:33.681 --> 00:14:37.603
And usually, which we're
going to see later,

00:14:37.603 --> 00:14:39.977
that means you can't sit down...

00:14:39.977 --> 00:14:43.825
if you have seen emptiness directly,

00:14:43.825 --> 00:14:44.975
and if a person says,

00:14:44.975 --> 00:14:46.906
"Look, just sit down
with me for five minutes

00:14:46.906 --> 00:14:48.972
and tell me what it is and I'll see it,"

00:14:48.972 --> 00:14:50.972
and that's not possible.

00:14:50.972 --> 00:14:55.199
So it cannot be put into
words in that sense.

00:14:55.199 --> 00:14:59.711
You cannot inspire an
immediate direct perception

00:14:59.711 --> 00:15:03.749
of emptiness in another person
just by talking about it.

00:15:03.749 --> 00:15:07.246
So BRJOD PAR BYA BA LDOG PA
STE means it's not something

00:15:07.246 --> 00:15:10.078
that could happen just
by talking about it.

00:15:10.078 --> 00:15:12.395
,SEMS KYI SPYOD YUL LDOG PAS SO,

00:15:12.395 --> 00:15:17.078
And that's because most people's
minds cannot conceptualize

00:15:17.078 --> 00:15:18.598
what you're talking about.

00:15:18.598 --> 00:15:20.518
You can sit down and describe emptiness

00:15:20.518 --> 00:15:24.563
for hour after hour for
them, but they won't be able

00:15:24.563 --> 00:15:27.338
to comprehend everything in such a way

00:15:27.338 --> 00:15:29.923
that they would see emptiness directly,

00:15:29.923 --> 00:15:34.464
within the next few hours.
That's usually not possible.

00:15:34.464 --> 00:15:37.370
It did happen at the first
turning of the Wheel -

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.953
but those people were ready.

00:15:39.953 --> 00:15:40.786
Why?

00:15:42.536 --> 00:15:45.394
They had eaten their teacher.

00:15:45.394 --> 00:15:46.624
(indistinct)

00:15:46.624 --> 00:15:48.542
But we're not getting into that

00:15:48.542 --> 00:15:51.602
and that's not a Buddhist practice.

00:15:51.602 --> 00:15:53.760
,MA SKYES PA DANG MA 'GAGS PA,

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:55.751
,CHOS NYID MYA NGAN 'DAS DANG MTSUNGS,

00:15:57.929 --> 00:16:01.846
In some respects, emptiness
is similar to nirvana.

00:16:03.714 --> 00:16:07.881
And this is the highest
interpretation of nirvana.

00:16:08.864 --> 00:16:12.892
We talk about it when we talk
about two kinds of nirvana:

00:16:12.892 --> 00:16:15.641
one is called nirvana
with something left over,

00:16:15.641 --> 00:16:18.506
and one is called nirvana
with nothing left over.

00:16:18.506 --> 00:16:23.506
And the lower schools think
that first you achieve nirvana

00:16:23.668 --> 00:16:27.720
with something left over -
meaning your physical body.

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:31.910
You permanently end your negative emotions,

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:34.386
and then later you die.

00:16:34.386 --> 00:16:36.393
And you die with that pure state of mind,

00:16:36.393 --> 00:16:41.393
but it's not like your body
blinks out or I guess it does, but anyway.

00:16:41.992 --> 00:16:43.989
First, you clean up your mind,

00:16:43.989 --> 00:16:45.260
and then you clean up your body.

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:47.834
So there is a period in your life

00:16:47.834 --> 00:16:49.783
that you haven't died yet,

00:16:49.783 --> 00:16:52.035
but you still have a
body that was created by

00:16:52.035 --> 00:16:53.957
karma and kleshas.

00:16:53.957 --> 00:16:55.891
And then the higher school
says, "No, no. That's not

00:16:55.891 --> 00:16:58.660
what nirvana with remainder means."

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:02.338
Nirvana without remainder happens first

00:17:02.338 --> 00:17:03.640
and that's the first...

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:06.748
those are the direct
perceptions of emptiness

00:17:06.748 --> 00:17:10.972
where you are no longer
loaded up with the idea

00:17:10.972 --> 00:17:12.588
that things come from their own side.

00:17:12.588 --> 00:17:14.796
While you are seeing emptiness directly,

00:17:14.796 --> 00:17:16.596
you are devoid of ideas

00:17:16.596 --> 00:17:18.407
that things could come
from their own side.

00:17:18.407 --> 00:17:21.390
During that less than twenty minutes,

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:23.298
you can't have a thought

00:17:23.298 --> 00:17:25.251
that things are coming
from their own side.

00:17:25.251 --> 00:17:28.072
Then you come out of the
direct perception of emptiness,

00:17:28.072 --> 00:17:32.130
and for seven more lifetimes, on some level,

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:34.779
you still feel like things
come from their own side,

00:17:34.779 --> 00:17:36.773
but you don't believe it.

00:17:36.773 --> 00:17:41.273
So what he's referring to
here is that kind of nirvana

00:17:42.718 --> 00:17:45.547
where for the twenty
minutes of direct perception

00:17:45.547 --> 00:17:50.130
of emptiness, you no longer
have starting and stopping

00:17:53.265 --> 00:17:54.662
in that sense.

00:17:54.662 --> 00:17:59.138
You are free of normal starting
coming from its own side,

00:17:59.138 --> 00:18:03.888
stopping from its own side, in that sense.

00:18:06.479 --> 00:18:08.921
By the way, I can't avoid teaching

00:18:08.921 --> 00:18:09.754
this paragraph because
Choney Lama refers to 

00:18:09.754 --> 00:18:10.587
the Diamond Cutter sutra.

00:18:17.452 --> 00:18:19.952
And he says, "By the way"
and it starts with RDOR GCOD.

00:18:22.117 --> 00:18:25.784
The paragraph starts with RDOR GCOD.

00:18:28.084 --> 00:18:30.292
Maybe Tim will show to you.

00:18:30.292 --> 00:18:31.989
By the way, he's doing an amazing job

00:18:31.989 --> 00:18:36.239
just digging out pieces of
texts and showing them to us.

00:18:37.931 --> 00:18:41.147
Let's read this together: RDOR
GCOD SOGS LAS SANGS RGYAS KYIS

00:18:41.147 --> 00:18:42.969
CHOS GANG YANG BSTAN PA MED

00:18:42.969 --> 00:18:45.099
"Look, I agree." "What?" "I agree that's what

00:18:45.099 --> 00:18:47.154
the Diamond Cutter sutra says."

00:18:47.154 --> 00:18:49.470
"What the Diamond Cutter sutra says?"

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:50.950
"The Diamond Cutter sutra says

00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:54.200
"the Buddhas never teach the dharma."

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:57.136
GANG YANG BSTAN PA MED means

00:18:57.136 --> 00:19:00.166
the Buddhas never teach any dharma.

00:19:00.166 --> 00:19:03.102
And he say, "OK, look, I know that's what the
Diamond Cutter sutra says."

00:19:03.102 --> 00:19:07.627
But, what it's saying is
he never teaches a dharma

00:19:07.627 --> 00:19:11.593
which is coming from its own side.

00:19:11.593 --> 00:19:15.176
Which means, when the
Buddha sat down in the

00:19:16.368 --> 00:19:19.709
Jetavan Garden in Vaishali? No.

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:25.543
Śrāvastī.

00:19:26.440 --> 00:19:30.348
When the Buddha sat down in
the Jetavan Garden at Śrāvastī

00:19:30.348 --> 00:19:34.773
and taught the dharma - none
of it was coming from him.

00:19:34.773 --> 00:19:38.860
The listeners who were there
had the seeds in their minds

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:41.984
to create a being who was
teaching them the path to freedom.

00:19:41.984 --> 00:19:44.984
And the generations of
people, the twenty five...

00:19:46.427 --> 00:19:49.926
Sorry, the hundred generations
of people after that

00:19:49.926 --> 00:19:52.882
who read the Diamond Cutter
sutra, were writing the sutra

00:19:52.882 --> 00:19:54.786
on the pages as they read.

00:19:54.786 --> 00:19:58.182
That's coming from you.
The sutra came from you.

00:19:58.182 --> 00:20:01.736
THA SNYAD DU NI SANGS RGYAS
KYIS BSTAN PAR 'DOD DGOS SO

00:20:01.736 --> 00:20:05.581
He says, "Look, on a conventional
level, we have to say..."

00:20:05.581 --> 00:20:06.836
THA SNYAD DU means

00:20:06.836 --> 00:20:08.934
'on a conventional level', we have to say

00:20:08.934 --> 00:20:10.818
the Buddha did teach the dharma.

00:20:10.818 --> 00:20:13.651
That's not what this verse is about.

00:20:13.651 --> 00:20:17.984
We're not denying that
the Buddha sat down

00:20:17.984 --> 00:20:22.067
in the Jetavan Garden and
taught the Diamond Cutter sutra.

00:20:22.067 --> 00:20:24.139
We're not saying that.

00:20:24.139 --> 00:20:25.552
We're not saying he never taught it.

00:20:25.552 --> 00:20:29.312
We're just saying that
nominally, conventionally speaking,

00:20:29.312 --> 00:20:30.645
he taught it,

00:20:30.645 --> 00:20:33.818
but if you look at it from
a karmic point of view,

00:20:33.818 --> 00:20:36.423
you taught the Diamond Cutter sutra.

00:20:36.423 --> 00:20:39.146
Anyone who ever heard it was teaching

00:20:39.146 --> 00:20:41.896
the Diamond Cutter sutra.

00:20:43.675 --> 00:20:48.425
That's starting a discussion
of using words to explain

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:54.727
a thing which is beyond words.

00:20:57.272 --> 00:21:02.097
Of those five great, sexy
subjects, we've now reached

00:21:02.097 --> 00:21:07.097
the third one, which is: DE KHO
NA NYID LA BKRI BA'I RIM PA

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:10.070
What a useful way to teach...

00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:11.367
BKRI BA means

00:21:11.367 --> 00:21:13.895
what's a useful way to guide people through

00:21:13.895 --> 00:21:15.474
the concepts of emptiness.

00:21:15.474 --> 00:21:16.557
BKRI BA means

00:21:16.557 --> 00:21:18.358
what's a useful way to guide people

00:21:18.358 --> 00:21:20.420
through these ideas.

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:21.253
And then he said,

00:21:22.803 --> 00:21:25.103
,THAMS CAD YANG DAG YANG DAG MIN,

00:21:25.103 --> 00:21:26.744
,YANG DAG YANG DAG MA YIN NYID,

00:21:26.744 --> 00:21:29.153
,YANG DAG MIN MIN YANG DAG YIN,

00:21:29.153 --> 00:21:32.045
,DE NI SANGS RGYAS RJES BSTAN PA'O,,

00:21:32.045 --> 00:21:32.878
And he starts playing with the word

00:21:32.878 --> 00:21:33.937
YANG DAG

00:21:33.937 --> 00:21:36.703
Say YANG DAG. What's the Sanskrit?

00:21:39.037 --> 00:21:39.870
Tathyaṃ, I guess,

00:21:41.403 --> 00:21:42.236
tathyaṃ.

00:21:44.603 --> 00:21:47.069
YANG DAG means 'pure', but the Sanskrit...

00:21:47.069 --> 00:21:50.052
it seems like he's using tathyaṃ,

00:21:50.052 --> 00:21:53.110
which means 'as it is'. tathya,

00:21:54.828 --> 00:21:57.386
like Tathagata, for example. Anyway.

00:22:01.666 --> 00:22:03.393
,THAMS CAD YANG DAG YANG DAG MIN,

00:22:03.393 --> 00:22:07.226
I mean, if you read the
line, here's how it sounds:

00:22:07.226 --> 00:22:10.622
"Everything is pure nothing is pure."

00:22:10.622 --> 00:22:13.039
"Purity is not pure perfectly."

00:22:15.438 --> 00:22:20.438
"That which is not pure is
the purity of what is not."

00:22:20.484 --> 00:22:25.166
"That's what the Buddha taught." (laughs)

00:22:25.166 --> 00:22:29.499
And the question is, I don't
know if we could go too much

00:22:31.076 --> 00:22:34.493
into this - it'll take a long time.

00:22:34.493 --> 00:22:35.493
Let's do it.

00:22:37.159 --> 00:22:39.219
In what sense did the Buddha

00:22:39.219 --> 00:22:41.476
teach the Diamond Cutter sutra?

00:22:41.476 --> 00:22:45.168
RGYAL BAS 'JIG RTEN RJES SU
GZHUG PA'I CHED DU THOG MAR MA

00:22:45.168 --> 00:22:47.334
RIG PAS BTAGS PA'I SNOD BCUD
THAMS CAD YANG DAG PA STE BDEN NO

00:22:47.334 --> 00:22:49.116
ZHES GSUNGS SHING DE
LTAR 'DZIN DU GZHUG GO

00:22:49.116 --> 00:22:51.765
In the beginning when the
Buddha first started to teach

00:22:51.765 --> 00:22:55.662
in this world, he did
describe in the Abhidharma

00:22:55.662 --> 00:23:00.136
what the world looks like,
how the world came into being.

00:23:00.136 --> 00:23:03.769
And in that sense, he
said the world is pure.

00:23:03.769 --> 00:23:07.769
But the word 'pure' here
in this verse means 'real'.

00:23:08.648 --> 00:23:11.729
So pure here means real.

00:23:11.729 --> 00:23:13.816
So did Buddha ever say the world was real?

00:23:13.816 --> 00:23:15.149
Yes. When?

00:23:15.149 --> 00:23:18.347
Like Abhidharma, in the third chapter.

00:23:18.347 --> 00:23:20.180
He describes all the continents.

00:23:20.180 --> 00:23:23.836
He describes the sun and the
moon. He describes the galaxy.

00:23:23.836 --> 00:23:27.827
He describes the different
solar systems - it's all real.

00:23:27.827 --> 00:23:30.840
Nowhere did he say all
this planets are not real.

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:33.081
In his first teaching.

00:23:33.081 --> 00:23:34.973
,DE LA PHYIS 'DUS BYAS

00:23:34.973 --> 00:23:37.190
'DI DAG SKAD CIG RE RE LA
'JIG PA'I GZHAN DU 'GYUR

00:23:37.190 --> 00:23:39.265
BA YOD PAS YANG DAG PA
MIN NO ZHES BSTAN LA,

00:23:39.265 --> 00:23:43.058
Then in his later teaching
he said, "But in a way

00:23:43.058 --> 00:23:45.474
things are in constant flux,

00:23:45.474 --> 00:23:48.505
"things never last for
more than a millisecond.

00:23:48.505 --> 00:23:51.704
"And in that sense, they are impure."

00:23:51.704 --> 00:23:55.066
They don't have purity
of being real for more

00:23:55.066 --> 00:23:56.150
than a millisecond.

00:23:56.150 --> 00:24:00.113
So let's call them unreal, in the
sense that they are fleeting

00:24:00.113 --> 00:24:02.780
and they are changing instant by instant.

00:24:04.928 --> 00:24:06.966
So did he ever say it was pure?

00:24:06.966 --> 00:24:07.799
Yes.

00:24:07.799 --> 00:24:09.471
Did he ever say it wasn't pure?

00:24:09.471 --> 00:24:10.304
Yes.

00:24:10.304 --> 00:24:11.541
Did he ever it was real?

00:24:11.541 --> 00:24:12.374
Yes.

00:24:12.374 --> 00:24:14.757
Then after that - just after
that - did he say it wasn't real?

00:24:14.757 --> 00:24:15.590
Yes.

00:24:16.784 --> 00:24:18.588
Now, it's not finished!

00:24:18.588 --> 00:24:20.271
DE NAS 'GA' ZHIG GI NGO BOR SNOD BCUD

00:24:20.271 --> 00:24:21.712
'DI DAG YANG DAG PA DANG,'PHAGS
PA'I RJES THOB KYI YE SHES LA

00:24:21.712 --> 00:24:24.464
BLTOS NAS YANG DAG PA MA YIN PA

00:24:24.464 --> 00:24:26.164
Then he changed his story and said,

00:24:26.164 --> 00:24:29.239
"For all you guys, the world is real,

00:24:29.239 --> 00:24:33.227
"but not for an Arya."

00:24:33.227 --> 00:24:36.790
For someone especially who is engaged

00:24:36.790 --> 00:24:41.455
in the direct perception of
emptiness, the world is not real.

00:24:41.455 --> 00:24:45.288
So far he said "real,"
then he said "unreal,"

00:24:46.486 --> 00:24:49.302
because it's momentary,
and then he said "real and unreal" 

00:24:49.302 --> 00:24:52.077
depends on who you are,

00:24:52.077 --> 00:24:54.152
depends on who's looking.

00:24:54.152 --> 00:24:57.522
So far we've got real, unreal,
and real and unreal.

00:24:57.522 --> 00:25:01.522
It's starting to make a
little more sense, right?

00:25:03.468 --> 00:25:06.168
ZAB MO LA MOS PA'I NGO BOR
'DUS BYAS RNAMS YANG DAG MIN PA STE

00:25:06.168 --> 00:25:08.567
SKAD CIG RE RE LA GZHAN DU
'GYUR PAR NGO BO NYID KYIS

00:25:08.567 --> 00:25:10.034
GRUB PA YANG MIN LA,

00:25:10.034 --> 00:25:11.584
YANG DAG PA STE SKAD CIG RE RE LA

00:25:11.584 --> 00:25:14.034
GZHAN 'GYUR BA MED PA YANG MIN NO
ZHES GNYIS KA BKAG STE

00:25:14.896 --> 00:25:18.554
Then those who were really
interested in emptiness,

00:25:18.554 --> 00:25:21.197
he changed his story.

00:25:21.197 --> 00:25:26.030
And he said, "Things that are
caused are not real." Why?

00:25:27.163 --> 00:25:30.697
Because by the time they're real,

00:25:30.697 --> 00:25:33.585
they change to something else. (laughs)

00:25:33.585 --> 00:25:36.718
Things that are caused are
not real because by the time

00:25:36.718 --> 00:25:40.187
they're real, they're not real anymore.

00:25:40.187 --> 00:25:42.803
'GYUR PAR NGO BO NYID
KYIS GRUB PA YANG MIN LA,

00:25:42.803 --> 00:25:44.395
YANG DAG PA STE

00:25:44.395 --> 00:25:46.275
From another point of view, they are real.

00:25:46.275 --> 00:25:48.747
SKAD CIG RE RE LA GZHAN 'GYUR BA MED PA

00:25:48.747 --> 00:25:53.330
In the instant that they
are themselves, they are real.

00:25:54.393 --> 00:25:58.399
But considered over
instants, they're unreal.

00:25:58.399 --> 00:25:59.732
In the instant they're real.

00:25:59.732 --> 00:26:03.545
Considered over a series of
instants, they are not real.

00:26:03.545 --> 00:26:04.962
Changed his story.

00:26:11.357 --> 00:26:15.413
Then Choney Lama makes a famous comment

00:26:15.413 --> 00:26:19.580
that different presentations
of what reality means

00:26:21.092 --> 00:26:24.038
to different levels of people is very much

00:26:24.038 --> 00:26:29.038
a Buddhist tradition because
people are at different levels.

00:26:29.110 --> 00:26:32.901
If you overwhelm a beginner student

00:26:32.901 --> 00:26:36.401
with too heavy a presentation of emptiness,

00:26:37.894 --> 00:26:39.776
you have mistaught them.

00:26:39.776 --> 00:26:42.316
You are a bad teacher.

00:26:42.316 --> 00:26:43.994
And Buddha is not a bad teacher.

00:26:43.994 --> 00:26:48.827
So Buddha would modify the
presentation to fit the student,

00:26:49.868 --> 00:26:52.387
even to the point of
saying things are not empty

00:26:52.387 --> 00:26:56.387
when they are, if it
would help the student.

00:26:59.921 --> 00:27:01.154
How are we doing on time?

00:27:01.154 --> 00:27:05.821
I'm going to keep going, Tim, into
what we had called class four.

00:27:08.078 --> 00:27:10.578
We're going to start studying...

00:27:11.860 --> 00:27:14.216
I'd like to go back to the Sanskrit

00:27:14.216 --> 00:27:16.392
and talk about some words that are useful

00:27:16.392 --> 00:27:19.438
for studying the next section.

00:27:19.438 --> 00:27:22.604
And the first one I'd like to talk about

00:27:22.604 --> 00:27:25.799
is lakṣaṇa.

00:27:25.799 --> 00:27:30.799
And I know Christina knows lakṣaṇa.

00:27:30.805 --> 00:27:33.845
Lakṣaṇa means... it's a difficult word

00:27:33.845 --> 00:27:35.645
and here it's going to mean

00:27:38.862 --> 00:27:41.012
'typical characteristic', MTSAN NYID.

00:27:43.222 --> 00:27:46.119
So lakṣaṇa means sign,

00:27:46.119 --> 00:27:48.595
but in logic it has
totally different names.

00:27:48.595 --> 00:27:51.266
It means kind of... what are the bright...

00:27:51.266 --> 00:27:53.585
like you're selling somebody a new car,

00:27:53.585 --> 00:27:56.791
what are the five lakṣaṇas?

00:27:56.791 --> 00:27:59.867
Oh, it's got a 700-horsepower engine,

00:27:59.867 --> 00:28:03.450
it's got six bold speakers...
These are lakṣaṇas,

00:28:04.800 --> 00:28:07.508
qualities of the new car that stand out:

00:28:08.741 --> 00:28:09.574
How do you say? Feature.

00:28:10.799 --> 00:28:15.132
Excuse me. Bright shiny
features of the new car.

00:28:16.210 --> 00:28:18.528
That's because lakṣ,

00:28:18.528 --> 00:28:21.778
which means to mark a thing as special.

00:28:24.754 --> 00:28:28.087
It comes from an Indo-European root leuk,

00:28:29.554 --> 00:28:33.004
leuk, which means light or brightness.

00:28:33.004 --> 00:28:35.004
I met a waiter... two days ago

00:28:35.004 --> 00:28:37.180
I said, "What's your name?"

00:28:37.180 --> 00:28:39.319
and he said, "Luke". I said,
"God, I was just studying

00:28:39.319 --> 00:28:42.683
"this verbal root! Do you
know what your name means?"

00:28:42.683 --> 00:28:44.757
And he says, "I have no idea."

00:28:44.757 --> 00:28:46.732
And I said, "I think it
means shining person.

00:28:46.732 --> 00:28:50.765
"You are a shining person."
He says, "I'll take it."

00:28:50.765 --> 00:28:54.396
So leuk is the Indo-European root.

00:28:54.396 --> 00:28:58.312
'Light' comes from that. That's
why there's a GH in light.

00:28:58.312 --> 00:29:02.443
Brightness comes from that,
that's why there's a GH.

00:29:02.443 --> 00:29:06.276
Rs and Ls are interchangeable, okay.

00:29:06.276 --> 00:29:10.365
I worked in... I built an office in Bangkok.

00:29:10.365 --> 00:29:12.373
We had three suppliers of gems,

00:29:13.957 --> 00:29:17.032
lear gems, real gems, and rare gems.

00:29:17.032 --> 00:29:20.182
Real gems, rare gems, and lear gems.

00:29:20.182 --> 00:29:23.733
But when the receptionist called me

00:29:23.733 --> 00:29:26.202
to tell me the salesman
was here, she said,

00:29:26.202 --> 00:29:27.792
"Leal gems is here."

00:29:27.792 --> 00:29:30.754
I said, "Which leal gems is here? Real?

00:29:30.754 --> 00:29:34.817
I said, "Leal?" So R and L
are basically interchangeable

00:29:34.817 --> 00:29:36.817
in Asian languages. And it's good.

00:29:38.201 --> 00:29:41.403
So leuk is the root

00:29:41.403 --> 00:29:43.633
and it actually it comes from ruc,

00:29:43.633 --> 00:29:44.466
which means to shine,

00:29:44.466 --> 00:29:46.132
and 'roach' comes from that.

00:29:46.132 --> 00:29:48.906
So anyway, light and luster and lucid

00:29:48.906 --> 00:29:51.573
are all cognates.

00:29:53.477 --> 00:29:55.227
I chose the two signs

00:29:59.318 --> 00:30:03.015
or bright shiny features, lakṣaṇa,

00:30:03.015 --> 00:30:06.053
of the Buddha which I
would consider the most

00:30:06.053 --> 00:30:10.405
important of the five that
he's going to present now.

00:30:10.405 --> 00:30:12.721
And I'll give you the Sanskrit for those.

00:30:12.721 --> 00:30:14.804
First one is śānta,

00:30:14.804 --> 00:30:16.419
which means peace,

00:30:16.419 --> 00:30:20.510
and it comes from a root śam.

00:30:20.510 --> 00:30:22.289
And you know the word śanti,

00:30:22.289 --> 00:30:25.357
and you know the word śamatha.

00:30:25.357 --> 00:30:27.148
śamatha is ZHI GNAS,

00:30:27.148 --> 00:30:29.699
which means to stay in peace.

00:30:29.699 --> 00:30:33.605
Probably stha, śamastha.

00:30:33.605 --> 00:30:36.355
If you are interested, most of the ancient

00:30:36.355 --> 00:30:39.280
sh- roots used to be KSH.

00:30:41.138 --> 00:30:44.654
Most of the ancient sh-
roots used to be KSH.

00:30:46.079 --> 00:30:49.829
And those come into
western languages as QU.

00:30:51.818 --> 00:30:55.226
So KSH is usually the real root

00:30:55.226 --> 00:30:59.059
when it starts with SH,
and most often the KSH

00:31:00.319 --> 00:31:04.319
comes into western languages
as QU, meaning quiet,

00:31:06.528 --> 00:31:10.419
or also calm. And kṣanti

00:31:10.419 --> 00:31:11.625
is patience.

00:31:11.625 --> 00:31:13.898
So I want you to learn śānta.

00:31:13.898 --> 00:31:14.731
Why?

00:31:14.731 --> 00:31:18.939
Because it's going to
be one of the five great

00:31:18.939 --> 00:31:20.687
lakṣaṇa of emptiness.

00:31:20.687 --> 00:31:23.062
It's going to be one of the five great

00:31:23.062 --> 00:31:25.181
selling points of emptiness.

00:31:25.181 --> 00:31:27.931
Like selling a new Tesla car or something.

00:31:28.847 --> 00:31:32.930
And another one I wanted
to teach you is actually

00:31:34.083 --> 00:31:36.961
a lack of prapañca.

00:31:36.961 --> 00:31:41.961
I like pañca, it means five.

00:31:42.061 --> 00:31:45.311
It came into the word finger, five.

00:31:47.781 --> 00:31:50.499
It came into the word fünf, in German,

00:31:50.499 --> 00:31:53.193
which comes from pañc.

00:31:53.193 --> 00:31:55.827
So fünf comes into English as five.

00:31:55.827 --> 00:32:00.747
So it means five, but what
it means is... look at my hand.

00:32:00.747 --> 00:32:05.747
It means, SPROS PA - the
verb means for light rays

00:32:06.922 --> 00:32:07.880
to spread out.

00:32:07.880 --> 00:32:11.151
We constantly see in those
tantric visualizations

00:32:11.151 --> 00:32:14.692
the world is coming out
of Vajra Yogini's heart. 

00:32:14.692 --> 00:32:16.275
There's this SPROS PA of light.

00:32:16.275 --> 00:32:18.105
SPROS PA means like

00:32:18.105 --> 00:32:19.720
you take your hand and you go like that.

00:32:19.720 --> 00:32:21.303
and that's pañca,

00:32:21.303 --> 00:32:22.570
that's prapañca.

00:32:22.570 --> 00:32:26.447
So pra- means forward, like
prow of a boat or proud,

00:32:26.447 --> 00:32:29.229
and prapañca means the world is

00:32:29.229 --> 00:32:31.907
a construct coming from you.

00:32:31.907 --> 00:32:34.773
It's a finger coming from
you, but a different one,

00:32:37.348 --> 00:32:38.181
five fingers. (laughs)

00:32:39.115 --> 00:32:41.356
Anyway, I'm not going to talk about that.

00:32:41.356 --> 00:32:44.553
I do have some self-control.

00:32:44.553 --> 00:32:48.261
So we are going to go through the five...

00:32:48.261 --> 00:32:52.428
these are the five shining
features of emptiness.

00:32:53.396 --> 00:32:56.779
I think that would be
enough for this class today.

00:32:56.779 --> 00:32:57.954
We'll go through the five features.

00:32:57.954 --> 00:33:00.387
They're in the next verse.

00:33:00.387 --> 00:33:02.920
,GZHAN LAS SHES MIN ZHI BA DANG,

00:33:02.920 --> 00:33:04.662
,SPROS PA RNAMS KYIS MA SPROS PA,

00:33:04.662 --> 00:33:06.345
,RNAM RTOG MED DON THA DAD MIN,

00:33:06.345 --> 00:33:09.203
,DE NI DE NYID MTSAN NYID DO,

00:33:12.547 --> 00:33:13.746
Here are the five

00:33:13.746 --> 00:33:15.219
and I'll read them off to you.

00:33:15.219 --> 00:33:19.136
Number one... and you can
leave that verse up, Tim.

00:33:21.412 --> 00:33:24.745
GZHAN GYIS BSTAN PA TZAM LAS
DNGOS SU SHES PA MIN GYI

00:33:26.103 --> 00:33:28.694
,GZHAN LAS SHES MIN means

00:33:30.371 --> 00:33:32.889
emptiness is not something
you can see directly

00:33:32.889 --> 00:33:36.081
by talking to someone directly.

00:33:36.081 --> 00:33:38.664
No one can sit down and trigger

00:33:40.859 --> 00:33:43.475
the direct perception of
emptiness in your mind

00:33:43.475 --> 00:33:47.660
just by talking to you
about what they saw.

00:33:47.660 --> 00:33:49.961
"So Geshe-la, you should never
have emptiness teachings."

00:33:49.961 --> 00:33:51.765
No, no. That's not the point.

00:33:51.765 --> 00:33:55.177
The point is, there's no
way for a person who has

00:33:55.177 --> 00:33:57.701
seen emptiness, no matter how desperately

00:33:57.701 --> 00:34:00.951
they might want to help you, they can't

00:34:02.442 --> 00:34:04.439
force you to see emptiness directly

00:34:04.439 --> 00:34:06.356
just by describing what they saw.

00:34:06.356 --> 00:34:08.397
In that sense, it cannot be

00:34:08.397 --> 00:34:10.789
communicated to another person directly.

00:34:10.789 --> 00:34:12.979
That's what we mean by directly.

00:34:12.979 --> 00:34:15.087
In the sense that if I explain it to you

00:34:15.087 --> 00:34:17.699
for ten minutes suddenly you see it.

00:34:17.699 --> 00:34:19.930
That's not going to happen.

00:34:19.930 --> 00:34:22.013
Does that mean we
shouldn't study emptiness?

00:34:22.013 --> 00:34:22.846
Duh, no.

00:34:24.313 --> 00:34:26.830
Of course you have to.

00:34:26.830 --> 00:34:29.861
So that's the first quality of emptiness.

00:34:29.861 --> 00:34:31.353
,GZHAN LAS SHES MIN

00:34:31.353 --> 00:34:34.755
Not something you could
directly or immediately

00:34:34.755 --> 00:34:37.799
learn from another person.

00:34:37.799 --> 00:34:42.799
ZHI BA means but it is a kind of peace.

00:34:42.801 --> 00:34:46.477
And it's not that you sit
down and feel peaceful.

00:34:46.477 --> 00:34:48.329
That's not what it means.

00:34:48.329 --> 00:34:49.496
'Peace' means...

00:34:53.029 --> 00:34:54.987
There's a joke, I mean the Sanskrit root

00:34:54.987 --> 00:34:58.320
śam, śāntiḥ also refers

00:34:58.320 --> 00:35:00.570
to 'wiping something out',

00:35:02.607 --> 00:35:06.274
like stopping it completely, put to rest,

00:35:07.110 --> 00:35:09.493
rest in peace.

00:35:09.493 --> 00:35:13.152
Rest in peace, meaning 'dead', 'finished'.

00:35:13.152 --> 00:35:16.410
So whenever you see śāntiḥ in Sanskrit,

00:35:16.410 --> 00:35:19.993
just be aware it also refers
to 'putting out a fire',

00:35:21.826 --> 00:35:25.144
the same word means putting out a fire.

00:35:25.144 --> 00:35:30.137
So making the fire leave existence.

00:35:30.137 --> 00:35:32.637
So that is what it means here.

00:35:33.615 --> 00:35:37.532
What fire does emptiness put out?

00:35:38.456 --> 00:35:41.497
The perception that the
bottle is coming from itself.

00:35:41.497 --> 00:35:44.655
A bottle that could come
from itself is permanently

00:35:44.655 --> 00:35:46.613
shut down, śāntiḥ.

00:35:46.613 --> 00:35:48.511
That's śāntiḥ, that's peace.

00:35:48.511 --> 00:35:52.761
So it doesn't mean the Eagle's
song "Peaceful easy feeling."

00:35:53.878 --> 00:35:56.321
It's not that at all.

00:35:56.321 --> 00:35:59.643
It's rather like putting out a car fire

00:35:59.643 --> 00:36:02.351
and saving the inhabitant of the car.

00:36:02.351 --> 00:36:07.315
Number three: ,SPROS
PA RNAMS KYIS MA SPROS PA,

00:36:07.315 --> 00:36:12.315
No prapañca, no...

00:36:12.848 --> 00:36:16.306
And here you have to call it constructs.

00:36:16.306 --> 00:36:19.493
No stories that
you make up in your head.

00:36:19.493 --> 00:36:23.195
Emptiness is free of stories
that you make up in your head.

00:36:23.195 --> 00:36:25.911
This is called elaborations.

00:36:25.911 --> 00:36:28.597
Some translators call it elaboration.

00:36:28.597 --> 00:36:30.236
I like to call it constructs.

00:36:30.236 --> 00:36:32.611
It means stuff made up in your head.

00:36:32.611 --> 00:36:36.111
Emptiness is free and he says specifically

00:36:37.208 --> 00:36:40.916
verbal elaborations or verbal constructs.

00:36:40.916 --> 00:36:45.499
It's not something you can
elaborate on with words

00:36:47.906 --> 00:36:49.739
and see it directly. That's
not going to happen.

00:36:49.739 --> 00:36:52.156
It's related to the first one.

00:36:54.803 --> 00:36:57.775
The fourth one was RNAM RTOG MED,

00:36:57.775 --> 00:37:00.025
which means no normal thought.

00:37:03.822 --> 00:37:08.239
Unthinkable with normal
thought. What? Emptiness. Why?

00:37:11.322 --> 00:37:13.755
When your mind is thinking normal thoughts,

00:37:13.755 --> 00:37:16.016
you can not see emptiness directly.

00:37:16.016 --> 00:37:18.211
So if there's a flow of
normal thoughts in your

00:37:18.211 --> 00:37:22.044
mind, it will stop the
perception of emptiness.

00:37:23.047 --> 00:37:25.295
And this refers to a contradiction,

00:37:25.295 --> 00:37:27.510
inherent contradiction.

00:37:27.510 --> 00:37:31.187
I give you, day after day, a
description of how the bottle

00:37:31.187 --> 00:37:33.687
is not coming from its own side.

00:37:33.687 --> 00:37:36.309
While I'm giving you that description,

00:37:36.309 --> 00:37:38.934
you are desperately holding to the idea

00:37:38.934 --> 00:37:42.103
that it's coming from the bottle.

00:37:42.103 --> 00:37:44.523
When I hold the bottle
up to tell you why it's

00:37:44.523 --> 00:37:47.032
not coming from the bottle, you are seeing

00:37:47.032 --> 00:37:50.956
it as coming from the
bottle until I put it down.

00:37:50.956 --> 00:37:54.595
And it's one of the big
contradictions of teaching

00:37:54.595 --> 00:37:56.277
emptiness.

00:37:56.277 --> 00:37:58.349
Even as you hold the pen up

00:37:58.349 --> 00:38:00.809
and explain why it's
not coming from itself,

00:38:00.809 --> 00:38:04.155
there's no one in the
audience who doesn't feel

00:38:04.155 --> 00:38:06.802
that it's coming from itself.

00:38:06.802 --> 00:38:08.635
It's just the way that it is.

00:38:08.635 --> 00:38:12.681
If you tell him ten thousand times,
you might have some hope.

00:38:12.681 --> 00:38:14.639
But the first ten thousand times,

00:38:14.639 --> 00:38:17.045
when they see the pen,
they automatically think

00:38:17.045 --> 00:38:19.257
it's coming from itself,
even as you explain how

00:38:19.257 --> 00:38:21.605
it's not coming itself.

00:38:21.605 --> 00:38:24.387
And that's what he's talking about here.

00:38:24.387 --> 00:38:27.285
Normal flow of thought is interrupted.

00:38:27.285 --> 00:38:28.118
Number five:

00:38:28.118 --> 00:38:30.843
CHOS THAMS CAD KYI DE KHO
NA NYID RIGS MTSUNGS PAS

00:38:30.843 --> 00:38:32.926
DON THA DAD PA MIN PA STE

00:38:32.926 --> 00:38:34.166
When we explain the diamond

00:38:34.166 --> 00:38:36.128
in the Diamond Cutter sutra,

00:38:36.128 --> 00:38:39.103
we often talk about
this particular quality

00:38:39.103 --> 00:38:42.111
of emptiness, which is that all objects

00:38:42.111 --> 00:38:43.770
have their own emptiness.

00:38:43.770 --> 00:38:47.854
All objects are devoid
of not coming from you.

00:38:47.854 --> 00:38:51.021
All objects in the universe are devoid

00:38:52.138 --> 00:38:54.712
of not coming from you.

00:38:54.712 --> 00:38:57.246
All husbands in the kitchen are empty

00:38:57.246 --> 00:38:59.157
of not coming from you.

00:38:59.157 --> 00:39:01.615
Which is to say, all
husbands in the kitchen

00:39:01.615 --> 00:39:02.991
are coming from you.

00:39:02.991 --> 00:39:05.800
That is their dependent origination.

00:39:05.800 --> 00:39:07.991
But to state it emptiness-way:

00:39:07.991 --> 00:39:12.430
no husband in the kitchen
is not coming from you.

00:39:12.430 --> 00:39:14.357
CHOS THAMS CAD KYI DE KHO
NA NYID RIGS MTSUNGS PAS

00:39:14.357 --> 00:39:17.190
In that sense, all objects in the universe

00:39:17.190 --> 00:39:19.107
are totally equal.

00:39:20.185 --> 00:39:23.518
So Buddha's saying constantly - equanimity,

00:39:25.408 --> 00:39:26.741
but there is a higher...

00:39:26.741 --> 00:39:29.453
treat all the people the same,
see all the people the same,

00:39:29.453 --> 00:39:31.961
but there's a higher form of equanimity,

00:39:31.961 --> 00:39:34.802
which we don't talk about very often,

00:39:34.802 --> 00:39:39.202
which is that you should
see all objects as equal

00:39:39.202 --> 00:39:42.232
in that they are coming equally from you.

00:39:42.232 --> 00:39:44.290
They all share a certain quality

00:39:44.290 --> 00:39:46.923
that they are coming from you.

00:39:46.923 --> 00:39:48.006
And there's many stories

00:39:48.006 --> 00:39:51.589
in scripture of a
teacher handing a student

00:39:53.131 --> 00:39:57.089
a little piece of dog
poop, or a piece of meat,

00:39:57.089 --> 00:39:58.448
or glass of wine,

00:39:58.448 --> 00:40:01.335
and saying, "Take a drink or taste it."

00:40:01.335 --> 00:40:02.168
And the student will say,
"No! It's poo-poo."

00:40:02.168 --> 00:40:03.001
Lama Pelma used to do it.

00:40:08.134 --> 00:40:10.467
The student said, "I'm
totally into emptiness."

00:40:10.467 --> 00:40:12.975
She said, "Okay, eat the poo-poo then."

00:40:12.975 --> 00:40:15.808
And some brave students tried.

00:40:15.808 --> 00:40:18.333
By the way, I'm not to recommending that.

00:40:18.333 --> 00:40:22.626
I'm not teaching that. I'm
not asking you to do that.

00:40:22.626 --> 00:40:24.878
And it's a pity I have to repeat that.

00:40:24.878 --> 00:40:26.211
But the point is

00:40:29.236 --> 00:40:32.836
dog poo-poo does have its own emptiness.

00:40:32.836 --> 00:40:37.602
And from that point of
view, it might be worth it

00:40:37.602 --> 00:40:40.852
to taste dog poo-poo every once in a while,

00:40:41.701 --> 00:40:45.854
just so you can say,
"This does have

00:40:45.854 --> 00:40:48.369
"the same quality as emptiness."

00:40:48.369 --> 00:40:50.077
Or "This does have the same quality

00:40:50.077 --> 00:40:51.858
"as Nagarjuna's great Wisdom."

00:40:51.858 --> 00:40:54.905
They all share a certain high quality

00:40:54.905 --> 00:40:57.679
in that they don't come from themselves.

00:40:57.679 --> 00:41:00.547
So the reason these tantric yogis

00:41:00.547 --> 00:41:04.274
why they do strange things
is to remind themselves,

00:41:04.274 --> 00:41:07.684
like in tasting poo-poo,
which I don't recommend

00:41:07.684 --> 00:41:09.934
and I'm not teaching that.

00:41:12.324 --> 00:41:14.686
The only way you could
do it, is if you were

00:41:14.686 --> 00:41:17.686
reflecting on something deeper:
(laughs)

00:41:17.686 --> 00:41:20.353
this, too, is not not coming from you.

00:41:23.405 --> 00:41:26.572
So those are the five great qualities.

00:41:28.136 --> 00:41:30.449
Those are the five great lakṣaṇa

00:41:30.449 --> 00:41:31.907
of emptiness,

00:41:31.907 --> 00:41:34.159
and they're very, very beautiful.

00:41:34.159 --> 00:41:38.159
And these are traditionally
taught by Nagarjuna.

00:41:42.623 --> 00:41:45.956
Next, we're going to
get into how the world

00:41:47.345 --> 00:41:49.549
might misunderstand emptiness.

00:41:49.549 --> 00:41:52.296
That's the next topic
that we'll be covering

00:41:52.296 --> 00:41:56.046
in the next class from
the eighteenth chapter,

00:41:57.253 --> 00:41:59.428
tenth verse.

00:41:59.428 --> 00:42:00.890
All right, see you then.
We're going slower than

